-- The Ewaipanomas R.C.C., Rifts World Book 6: South America p.102-103.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/add-ewaipanomas-class.sql
--
-- Generated by scripts/class-check.mjs --emit-script from a validated draft.
-- Apostrophes are doubled and non-ASCII is spliced with char(); CR is stripped.
-- Run class-check on THIS file before applying - the ASCII/CRLF pre-flight only
-- fires against the real artifact.


-- The class itself. INSERT ... WHERE NOT EXISTS rather than INSERT OR IGNORE,
-- so re-running the script is a no-op instead of a silent partial write.
INSERT INTO imported_classes (class_id, name, system, markdown, status, created_by)
SELECT 'ewaipanomas', 'Ewaipanomas', 'rifts', '---
id: ewaipanomas
name: Ewaipanomas
system: rifts
source_book: Rifts World Book 6: South America p.102-103
category: rcc
men_of_arms: false
attribute_dice:
  IQ: "3d6"
  ME: "3d6+4"
  MA: "3d6"
  PS: "2d6+20"
  PP: "3d6"
  PE: "4d6+4"
  PB: "2d6"
  Spd: "3d6"
mdc_base: "2d6x10 plus 1d6 per level"
xp_table: [0, 2181, 4341, 8681, 17461, 27201, 37301, 53401, 75501, 99601, 143701, 186801, 238901, 298001, 358001]
bonuses:
  saves: { spell_magic: 2, ritual_magic: 2, psionics: 2, horror_factor: 2 }
  pools: { sdc: "1d6x10+10", ppe: "1d4x10" }
natural_abilities:
  - { name: "Supernatural Strength and Endurance", description: "Both P.S. and P.E. are supernatural." }
  - { name: "Bio-Regeneration", description: "Regenerates 2D6 M.D.C. per hour." }
  - { name: "Communicate with Elementals", description: "98%." }
  - { name: "Headless Anatomy", description: "No head: the eyes sit on the shoulders and there are two mouths, one in the middle of each breast." }
restrictions:
  - "Cybernetics: never get any."
  - "Occupations: 70% of all Ewaipanomas are Earth Warlocks, 20% are Stone Masters and 10% follow other O.C.C.s. The book does not forbid any occupation, so none is closed here."
  - "Average level of experience is 1D4. Their casual, laid-back nature makes them advance at half the normal rate; some adventurers and elders reach much higher levels."
  - "Size: 6 to 7 feet tall (1.8 to 2.1 m). Weight: 300 lbs (135 kg)."
  - "Standard equipment varies with the O.C.C."
side_effects: "Normally calm, rational and diplomatic, an Ewaipanomas who loses his temper - provoked by brutality or the threat of slavery - is a terrible sight."
extraction_notes: |
  Read from the text-layer cache p103-p104 (printed 102-103) and checked against
  a render of printed 103. The race''s stat block is on printed 103; its
  introduction starts on 102.

  Attributes as printed. The book calls strength and endurance supernatural;
  that is a natural ability in prose here, since supernatural P.S./P.E. is not
  a field.

  S.D.C./Hit Points: "Standard hit points in non-M.D.C. worlds, plus
  1D6x10+10 S.D.C. (plus those gained by O.C.C. and skills)" - stored as a pool
  BONUS (bonuses.pools.sdc), not sdc_base, because it adds to the occupation''s.
  No hit_points_base is stated: "standard" is the core formula.

  M.D.C.: 2D6x10 plus 1D6 per level in a mega-damage environment, stored as
  mdc_base with the per-level growth in the formula.

  men_of_arms: false - a race that states no S.D.C. or M.D.C. base formula of
  the occupation kind (its S.D.C. is a bonus on top of the O.C.C.''s).

  Bonuses: "+2 to save vs magic and psionics" is stored as +2 to spell magic,
  ritual magic and psionics; "+2 to save vs horror factor" as horror_factor 2;
  "add 1D4x10 to starting P.P.E." as a P.P.E. pool bonus, since the book says it
  adds to the O.C.C.''s. No ppe_base and no isp_base: the race prints neither.
  No psionics block - the book states no psionics, so the standard roll applies.

  O.C.C.s: 70% Earth Warlock (warlock-earth), 20% Stone Master (stone-master),
  10% others. The book gives a distribution, not a restriction, so no
  occ_restrictions is stored and the table is prose under restrictions and the
  GM Notes.

  Experience: the book prints an "Ewaipanoma" ladder in the experience tables
  on printed 168 (cache p169), confirmed on a render - not 169. Stored as the 15
  lower bounds. The page''s own note says a race that takes an O.C.C. uses the
  O.C.C.''s table, which is how a pairing already composes; this ladder applies
  when the race is played alone. The "half the normal rate" line on the race
  page is kept as prose rather than applied a second time on top of a ladder
  the book prints for the race.

  No skills of any kind: an R.C.C. that takes an O.C.C. gets its skills from
  the occupation.
---

## Lore

European explorers of the Amazon came home with tales of a jungle tribe with
no heads at all: brown-skinned human bodies, eyes set in the shoulders, and a
mouth in the middle of each breast. The stories were dismissed as heat,
fever and superstition. They were true.

The Ewaipanomas are not native to Earth. Some two thousand of them were
wrenched from their homeworld - a place bound closely to earth elementals and
poor in plant and animal life - by the dimensional disaster the ancient
Atlanteans caused, and dropped into the South American jungle. Earth''s riot of
life drove many to the edge of madness, and with magic ebbing at the time
their elemental powers, once the equal of an earth warlock''s, were much
diminished. Strength and toughness kept them alive against the jungle and
against native tribes who took them for demons.

A few peaceful tribes took them in and taught them the rain forest. Later
tribes hunted them nearly to extinction, until the Skellian Atlanteans arrived
and saved them. Most now live among the Atlanteans of Manoa, where their power
over earth and stone helped build the city; many remain builders, architects
and stone masters there, a magic they learned from the Manoans.

They are a calm, deliberate, rational people who think things through, and
those of Manoa are well educated and fond of logic. Brutality or a threat of
slavery can break that calm, and the result is fearsome.

## GM Notes

Occupation table: 70% of Ewaipanomas are Earth Warlocks, 20% are Stone
Masters, and 10% follow other O.C.C.s. Average experience level is 1D4, though
adventurers and elders can climb far higher; the race''s laid-back nature is
the book''s reason they advance slowly. They never take cybernetics.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ewaipanomas');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ewaipanomas';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
